<!doctype html><html><head><meta charset='utf-8'><style>body{font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt}h1{text-align:center;font-size:18pt}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%}th,td{border:1px solid #333;padding:6px;vertical-align:top}th{background:#d9eaf7}h2{font-size:12pt}</style></head><body>
<h1>Software Requirements Specification</h1><h2>Problem Statement #26: Peer-to-Peer Carpooling &amp; Expense Splitter</h2>
<table><tr><th>Req ID</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th><th>Priority</th><th>Acceptance Criteria (measurable pass/fail)</th><th>Rationale</th></tr>
<tr><td>FR-001</td><td>Functional</td><td>The system shall calculate route compatibility between a driver and passenger and permit a match only when the additional detour is at most 1.5 km.</td><td>High</td><td>Pass: a route with detour ≤1.5 km is marked compatible; Fail: a route with detour &gt;1.5 km is accepted.</td><td>Prevents impractical matches and follows the stated tolerance.</td></tr>
<tr><td>FR-002</td><td>Functional</td><td>The system shall allow a Driver Host to publish a recurring or one-time ride with origin, destination, departure time, seats, and detour tolerance.</td><td>High</td><td>Pass: all five fields validate and the ride appears in the driver's list; Fail: missing/invalid data prevents publication.</td><td>Provides the supply of rides passengers can discover.</td></tr>
<tr><td>FR-003</td><td>Functional</td><td>The system shall allow a Rider Commuter to search compatible rides by route and date, view ride details, and submit a join request.</td><td>High</td><td>Pass: search returns only rides matching date and tolerance, and a valid request changes status to Pending; Fail: incompatible rides are shown or request is not recorded.</td><td>Core passenger discovery and booking function.</td></tr>
<tr><td>FR-004</td><td>Functional</td><td>The system shall allow the Driver Host to accept or decline a rider request and notify both parties of the decision.</td><td>High</td><td>Pass: decision is stored and in-app notifications reach driver and rider within 10 seconds; Fail: status or notification is missing.</td><td>Confirms participation and avoids uncertain travel plans.</td></tr>
<tr><td>FR-005</td><td>Functional</td><td>The system shall calculate each rider's fuel-cost share for a confirmed ride and display the amount to all participants.</td><td>High</td><td>Pass: displayed shares sum to the configured total fuel cost (within ₹0.01) and are visible after confirmation; Fail: sum differs or a participant cannot view it.</td><td>Delivers the expense-splitting purpose transparently.</td></tr>
<tr><td>NFR-001</td><td>Nonfunctional (Security)</td><td>User ratings, driving-license verification documents, and travel histories shall be stored securely with encrypted backups and access control.</td><td>High</td><td>Pass: data is encrypted at rest/in backup, TLS is used in transit, and unauthorized-account tests receive HTTP 403/denial; Fail: any protected artifact is readable without authorization.</td><td>Protects sensitive identity and travel information.</td></tr>
<tr><td>NFR-002</td><td>Nonfunctional (Performance/Availability)</td><td>The system shall return 95% of route searches within 3 seconds and maintain at least 99.5% monthly availability.</td><td>Medium</td><td>Pass: load test records p95 search latency ≤3 s and monitoring shows uptime ≥99.5% over a 30-day period; Fail: either threshold is missed.</td><td>Supports reliable use during commuting peaks.</td></tr>
</table></body></html>
